        {
            "block_label": "figure_title",
            "block_content": "<div style=\"text-align: center;\">Figure 3: Donor-matched within-cell-type contamination effect across three foundation models. (a) Per-pair tightness gap (each dot is one (cell-type, donor) pair from the pancreatic islet benchmark); black bar marks the mean. UCE-4L shows the largest effect. (b) Real mean gap (solid) versus permutation null mean (hatched) for each model, with  $ n_{+}/n $ sign-test counts and permutation p-values annotated. All three models exceed their null at  $ p \\leq 0.03 $.</div>\n",
            "block_bbox": [
